cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the reported measurements, please cite it."
title: "LLM-directed weight-space programming on a network encoder"
abstract: >-
  Closed-form, gradient-free weight-space interventions on snlucsb/netFound-small.
  A rank-1 edit of one tensor produces a linear, monotone increase in between-class
  representation distance (2x at the strongest edit) with zero change in downstream
  nearest-centroid decisions, because the edit scales the class means and their
  ambiguous members together.
